  "prefLabel": "Ph 703.11 Acts Prohibited",
  "priorExpiration": "2020-11-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ph 703.11 Acts Prohibited. Splitting fees, making rebates, or sharing money received for pharmaceutical services, or the donation of or the use of equipment with other health practitioners or with health institutions providing patient care shall be deemed by the board to be contrary to the best interests of the patient, and shall therefore be prohibited.\n\nSource. #6181-B, eff 2-5-96; amd by #6933, eff 2-1-99; paragraphs (a), (b), (d), and (e) EXPIRED: 2-5-04; amd by #8316, eff 3-26-05; intro. paragraph and (c) EXPIRED: 2-1-07; paragraphs (a), (b), (d), and (e) EXPIRED: 3-26-13\n\nNew. #10903, eff 8-5-15; amd by #13007, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 3-20-20; amd by #13043, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 5-20-20, EXPIRED 11-16-20 (in intro. and paragraph (c)); ss by #13398, eff 6-22-22 (formerly Ph 704.16) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ph 700)",
